# cargo-fuzz build output.
target/

# The working corpus. libFuzzer writes every coverage-increasing input here,
# which after a short campaign is thousands of mutated files — memory for the
# fuzzer, noise in a repository. Regenerate the seeds with ./seed_corpus.sh;
# the coverage memory is worth keeping on the machine that does the soaking,
# not in the history.
corpus/

# artifacts/ is deliberately NOT ignored. A crash reproducer is the most
# valuable thing a fuzz run produces, and tests/fuzz_corpus_tests.rs replays
# every file in it on STABLE — so a finding outlives the nightly toolchain
# that found it, and comes back as an ordinary test failure if it regresses.
